# Minimal page UI

DataDungeon pages should feel **clean and minimal**. Prefer scannable layouts over prose.

## Page headers

- Use `PageHeader` with **title only** unless one short line is truly needed for context (e.g. empty-state or error routes).
- **Do not** add `description` props that explain how filters, smart lists, chips, or fields relate to each other. Users learn by using the UI.
- **Do not** add tutorial paragraphs under titles (“set that in Edit contact”, “open Filters for…”, etc.).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — meta-explanation under the title
<PageHeader
  title="Contacts"
  description="Smart list chips mostly match Contact category…"
/>

// ✅ GOOD — title + actions only
<PageHeader title="Contacts" actions={…} />
```

## Copy elsewhere on pages

- Skip redundant helper text above lists, toolbars, and filter bars when labels, placeholders, and empty states are enough.
- Keep dialog **titles** specific; avoid long **descriptions** unless confirming a destructive action or a non-obvious workflow.
- Empty states: one short line + primary action — not a paragraph.
- Prefer tooltips on icon buttons over inline “how to use this” paragraphs.

## When text is OK

- Validation errors and toasts
- Legal/privacy notices (e.g. print DOB checkbox)
- genuinely non-obvious one-liners in empty states (max ~1 sentence)

When in doubt, remove the text.
